{title: Midnight Special}
{artist: Traditional}
{key: G}

{c: Verse 1}
[G]Well, you wake up in the morning, hear the ding-dong [C]ring,
You go [G]marching to the table, see the same old [D7]thing.
Ain't no [G]food upon the table, and no pork up in the [C]pan,
But you [G]better not complain, boy, you'll [D7]get in trouble with the [G]man.

{c: Chorus}
Let the [G]Midnight Special shine a light on [C]me,
Oh let the [G]Midnight Special shine a light on [D7]me.
Let the [G]Midnight Special shine a light on [C]me,
Oh let the [G]Midnight Special shine its [D7]ever loving light on [G]me.

{c: Verse 2}
[G]Yonder comes Miss Rosie, how in the world do you [C]know?
Well I [G]know her by her apron and the dress she [D7]wore.
Umbrella [G]on her shoulder, piece of paper in her [C]hand,
Well she [G]come to see the governor, she wants to [D7]free her [G]man.
